      <li>The prose of this website, including the methodology and <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a>: CC BY 4.0.</li>
      <li>Excerpts of scanned servers' source, quoted as evidence, remain their authors'; no licence to them is granted.</li>
      <li>Each server's install-resolution block is deps.dev's data (Open Source Insights) and stays under CC BY 4.0, attributed to deps.dev.</li>
      <li>The mcpwatchman name and mark are not licensed; all rights reserved.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The <a href="https://github.com/kVadrum/mcpwatchman/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE file</a>{" "}
      is canonical for what falls where.
    </p>
    <p>KeMeK&nbsp;Network &copy; 2026</p>
  </section>

  <section class="doc-section" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
    <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      To report a mistake in the methodology or a wrong number, open an{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/kVadrum/mcpwatchman/issues">issue</a> —
      adversarial contributions are the most useful kind. To contest a
      finding, see <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure and appeals</a>. To report
      a vulnerability in mcpwatchman itself, use the{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/kVadrum/mcpwatchman/security/advisories/new">private advisory form</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Doc>
